WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.280
And looking at the
landscape with new eyes,

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:03.940
this was not a kind of place I'm used to.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:06.180
Rivers appeared and disappeared

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:09.020
going under and rising
back to the surface.

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:12.370
And these sinkholes, where
the rivers go back in

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.900
or where they come out is where

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.713
most of the evidence comes from.

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:18.710
We found this in the woods.

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:21.760
Water welling up from
below, and down inside

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.990
there'll be artifacts and bones.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:26.240
Divers have excavated these holes,

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:29.750
finding entire stomach
contents of a Mastodon,

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:31.850
parts of every animal that lived here,

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:34.510
and numerable artifacts from the Ice Age.

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:36.770
We cannon-balled
into this particular one,

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:39.840
and I remember the
current tugging at my feet

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.260
and how dark it was when I looked down.

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:44.713
Shadows falling into shadows.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:48.360
One researcher described
diving in one of these holes

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:52.090
with another excavator and
pulling a long ivory shaft

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:55.110
out of a crack --part of a throwing weapon--

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:56.220
and he was so excited

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:58.840
that he was shouting over his regulator.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:01.830
And another diver told
me about drifting down

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:03.950
to the bottom with a weight belt

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:06.830
and it's being completely
black down there,

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:09.030
flicking on a thousand watt light,

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:11.970
and the megafauna bones
were all around him,

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:13.713
glowing like gold.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:17.750
I think of these as emergence places,

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:21.430
spots on the land where the
Ice Age pokes up through.

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:24.010
This is the Gault site in central Texas,

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:28.053
and it has human artifacts
going back 25,000 years.

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:34.370
I walked down into this pit
and I was going layer by layer,

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:37.900
going down through time,
and the lower I got,

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:41.310
the more of the ground of
the trenches became wet.

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:43.620
And there were generators going

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:46.460
and hoses pumping water back out

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:50.340
because this was cut down
below the water table,

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:55.340
down to where people left
artifacts 25,000 years ago.

00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:56.980
If the pump stopped running,

00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:00.880
this would just fill up
like a swimming pool.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:04.320
And of course, I'm thinking
about the old stories down here

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:07.920
about the old Diné man who told me

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:10.450
that the people came from the ground.

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:12.150
So many of those original stories

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:14.450
are about this watery underworld.

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:17.270
And I thought, is this the
place they're talking about?

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.363
Is this one of the emergence sites?

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:23.236
We got into the bags of artifacts

00:02:23.236 --> 00:02:26.260
and found the oldest one there,

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:28.900
the last artifact that had been picked up.

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:32.550
This is a core left
behind from manufacturer.

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:34.820
But you hold it and you think,

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:36.360
at the time I was there,
they were only down

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:40.100
to the 15,000-year layer,
and I was thinking,

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:44.460
this was touched by
somebody 15,000 years ago.

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:47.650
This thing felt like a time machine.

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:50.110
People arrived in this continent

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:52.550
and then went everywhere.

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:56.310
And this rock was still
wet, as if from birth.

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:58.643
(deep gong)

